---
import PageShell from '../../../layouts/PageShell.astro';

const seoTitle = 'Review Reply Templates for Med Spas';
const seoDesc =
	'Review reply templates for med spas with privacy-safe response patterns for positive, mixed, delayed, and dissatisfied reviews.';
---

<PageShell title={seoTitle} description={seoDesc}>
	<h1>Review Reply Templates for Med Spas</h1>
	<p>
		Public review replies should sound human without confirming patient details. Use these as drafting
		patterns, then adapt them to the clinic's voice and compliance process.
	</p>

	<h2>Reply templates</h2>
	<table>
		<thead>
			<tr>
				<th>Review type</th>
				<th>Draft reply</th>
				<th>Why it works</th>
			</tr>
		</thead>
		<tbody>
			<tr>
				<td>Warm positive</td>
				<td>Thank you for sharing this. Our team is grateful for the opportunity to support patients with care, clarity, and follow-through.</td>
				<td>Appreciative, but does not confirm a service or visit detail.</td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td>Mentions staff</td>
				<td>We appreciate your kind words about the team. We will share this internally, and we are glad the experience felt supportive.</td>
				<td>Recognizes staff praise without adding private context.</td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td>Mixed experience</td>
				<td>Thank you for taking the time to share this. We would value the chance to understand the concern directly through our private follow-up channel.</td>
				<td>Moves details out of public view while sounding accountable.</td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td>Delay or scheduling issue</td>
				<td>We are sorry the timing did not meet expectations. Please contact our team directly so we can review what happened and improve the experience.</td>
				<td>Owns the experience without debating publicly.</td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td>Highly dissatisfied</td>
				<td>We take concerns seriously and would like to review this through the appropriate private channel. Please contact our office manager so we can follow up.</td>
				<td>Calm, direct, and avoids clinical discussion.</td>
			</tr>
		</tbody>
	</table>

	<h2>Before publishing a reply</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>Remove any treatment confirmation, appointment detail, diagnosis, or outcome discussion.</li>
		<li>Keep the tone appreciative and brief.</li>
		<li>Use a private channel for details, especially when the review is negative or medically specific.</li>
		<li>Do not offer incentives, discounts, or public compensation in exchange for edits.</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>Example adjustment</h2>
	<div class="example-box">
		<p>
			Instead of "We are glad your Botox appointment went well," use "We are glad the experience felt
			supportive." The second version expresses appreciation without confirming a specific treatment.
		</p>
	</div>

	<div class="warning-box">
		<strong>Privacy note:</strong> these are drafting examples only. Review replies should follow platform
		rules, HIPAA-aware communication practices, and the clinic's legal/compliance guidance.
	</div>
</PageShell>
